    ($SATQ$68f343c9$SATQ$, $SATQ$d6701d8a-79c5-4cbd-b549-dcd4b570f33b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">If&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals x plus 6"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 6 x"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></math>, what is the value of&nbsp;<math alttext="7 f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis minus g left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a08feb7f-3684-4f81-a3e3-78c2c3c9b9bc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"760a807d-ee5f-46f7-b49a-e63d80cc7a13","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0c675bc6-4212-4344-bce8-0f452115a138","content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fc45f8af-1d33-408e-aa01-016cc66b895c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["fc45f8af-1d33-408e-aa01-016cc66b895c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It's given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals x plus 6"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in the function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals 2 plus 6"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals 8"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. It's also given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 6 x"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in the function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g"><mi>g</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals 12"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="12"><mn>12</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="g left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis minus g left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mn>7</mn><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis minus 12"><mn>7</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>12</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="44"><mn>44</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis minus g left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis"><mn>7</mn><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="44"><mn>44</mn></math>.</p>
