</math> feet. What is the length, in feet, of the rug?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["15"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["15"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn>
</math>. It's given that the equation <math alttext="46 equals 2 x plus 2 y"><mrow>
	<mn>46</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<mi>y</mi>
		</mrow>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> gives the perimeter of a rectangular rug that has length <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, in feet, and width <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, in feet. It's also given that the width of the rug is <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> feet. Substituting <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="46 equals 2 x plus 2 y"><mrow>
	<mn>46</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<mi>y</mi>
		</mrow>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="46 equals 2 x plus 2 left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis"><mn>46</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="46 equals 2 x plus 16"><mrow>
	<mn>46</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>16</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="16"><mn>16</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="30 equals 2 x"><mrow>
	<mn>30</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>2</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="15 equals x"><mrow>
	<mn>15</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Since <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents the length, in feet, of the rug, it follows that the length of the rug is <math alttext="15"><mn>15</mn>
</math> feet.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6a12efbb","external_id":"c2ed48a0-96b6-4990-b199-6a704301200c","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"a4aec96a-329b-4fe0-b6bb-26fec641f177","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"46 equals 2 x plus 2 y\"><mn>46</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math> gives the perimeter of a rectangular rug that has length <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, in feet, and width <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, in feet. The width of the rug is <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> feet. What is the length, in feet, of the rug?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["15"],"correct_answer":["15"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math>. It's given that the equation <math alttext=\"46 equals 2 x plus 2 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>46</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> gives the perimeter of a rectangular rug that has length <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, in feet, and width <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, in feet. It's also given that the width of the rug is <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> feet. Substituting <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"46 equals 2 x plus 2 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>46</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"46 equals 2 x plus 2 left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis\"><mn>46</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"46 equals 2 x plus 16\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>46</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"30 equals 2 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>30</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"15 equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represents the length, in feet, of the rug, it follows that the length of the rug is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math> feet.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357391,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"6a12efbb","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1730147357391,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"c2ed48a0-96b6-4990-b199-6a704301200c","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"a4aec96a-329b-4fe0-b6bb-26fec641f177","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[],"externalid":"c2ed48a0-96b6-4990-b199-6a704301200c","keys":["15"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math>. It's given that the equation <math alttext=\"46 equals 2 x plus 2 y\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>46</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</