</math>. Which system of equations describes this situation?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9ae9f565-dd37-463b-834a-08e047f310bb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"x plus 7 equals 2 y\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math></p>\n<p><math alttext=\"y equals x minus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"0cdbb23f-5556-428c-8ee6-9a7792e0c39c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"x plus 7 equals 2 y\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math></p>\n<p><math alttext=\"y equals 3 minus x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"41eb9298-2093-4015-b424-2126b9cdbf54","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis equals y\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math></p>\n<p><math alttext=\"y equals x minus 3\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"696753d2-1ea8-43a7-9aae-a1b3826e498e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis equals y\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math></p>\n<p><math alttext=\"y equals 3 minus x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9ae9f565-dd37-463b-834a-08e047f310bb"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that the sum of a number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7"><mn>7</mn></math> is twice as large as a number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>. This can be described by the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus 7 equals 2 y"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math> less than the number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math>. This can be described by the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals x minus 3"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Therefore, the system consisting of the equations <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus 7 equals 2 y"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals x minus 3"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> describes this situation.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 3 minus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math> describes a situation where the number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> less than <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis equals y"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math> describes a situation where the number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is twice the sum of a number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7"><mn>7</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. The equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis equals y"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math> describes a situation where the number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is twice the sum of a number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7"><mn>7</mn></math>, and the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 3 minus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math> describes a situation where a number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> less than <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3"><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6e50ce28","external_id":"6224ef79-ede3-42e9-82fc-447127d5e27e","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"a0d227c6-d92c-4471-95c4-155c97986d40","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.D.","skill_desc":"Systems of two linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The sum of a number <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> is twice as large as a number <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>. The number <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> less than the number <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>. Which system of equations describes this situation?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9ae9f565-dd37-46