</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5573fa4c-5957-4e5e-aa7c-8e395b63a2b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus 6 x plus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"80457800-aa6c-4379-9ea1-eaf15b76a9ea","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 6 x plus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2e97d098-61d1-442b-9939-552e780dea2b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 4 x minus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0b94ef52-e084-4b8f-973c-62e25976a775","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 4 x plus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0b94ef52-e084-4b8f-973c-62e25976a775"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane with a slope of <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and a <em>y</em>-intercept of <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma b right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> can be defined by an equation in the form <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that line <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> has a slope of <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> and passes through the point <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 6 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. It follows that <math alttext="m equals 4"><mrow>
	<mi>m</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="b equals 6"><mrow>
	<mi>b</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>.&nbsp;Substituting <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="y equals 4 x plus 6"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
